# Line endings are a repository property, not a per-developer git config. Without this file
# the tree is correct only for developers who happen to have core.autocrlf set, and the first
# contributor without it commits a whole-file CRLF diff.
#
# Everything currently in the index is LF, so this pins the status quo rather than changing it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Read by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Committed deterministic baselines. Written by the C telemetry writer with LF; keeping the
# worktree copy LF too means the file on disk is byte-identical to what the run produced.
*.csv text eol=lf

# Baselines are machine-generated and wide: a re-record is thousands of near-identical lines
# that nobody reads and that buries the real change in a review. Suppress the textual diff and
# mark them generated so forges collapse them by default. They stay TRACKED on purpose —
# `make regression` and `make verify` compare against them, so a clone without them has no
# regression gate. To inspect one deliberately: git diff --text -- tests/baselines/<file>.csv
tests/baselines/*.csv -diff linguist-generated

# Binary: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.a   binary
*.lib binary
